# DESK06 control run -- does NOT touch File -> Execute EmuCON. It answers the
# one question the wdef run left open: the two frame-corner pixels that differ
# between the window as `wind_open` drew it and the window as a whole-screen
# `redraw::redraw_desktop()` draws it.
#
# The control uses the *pre-existing* console-program path
# (`main::launch_native`, ftype::Flavor::Console -> clear_and_home, run,
# console_pause_for_key, redraw_desktop), which predates DESK06 and calls the
# very same `redraw_desktop`. `HELLO.NCP` is the first icon of the third row of
# the C:\ window (see wdef-F-back.png): centre about (95,190).
#
#   C: icon around (37,42). Any key ends the pause; SPACE = IKBD 39.
#
# (A first attempt used `Options -> Read .INF file...`; it returns early on
#  this card image because `load_and_apply()` rejects the 21-byte NEWDESK.INF,
#  so no redraw happened at all -- 0 differing pixels proved nothing.)
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 37 42
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
2900 mark B_WINDOW
3200 move 95 190
3400 down
3403 up
3410 down
3413 up
4600 mark C_PROGRAM
4900 key 39
4930 key b9
5600 move 600 240
6400 mark D_AFTER_NCP
